1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:02,228
- Auntie.
- I'm fine.

3
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:03,396
Just hurry.

4
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:13,907
- Auntie. I--
- Save the patient first.

5
00:01:14,991 --> 00:01:17,577
Just do the surgery. Su-jeong.

6
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:19,662
You can do this.

7
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:01,121
<i>Auntie,</i>

8
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:05,542
<i>on graduation day, you promised to teach</i>
<i>me how to do a multi-organ transplant.</i>

9
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:07,627
<i>You even said it had to be a solo surgery.</i>

10
00:02:08,294 --> 00:02:10,130
<i>Tell me what you said to me that day.</i>

11
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:13,591
<i>There is no one else.</i>

12
00:02:14,425 --> 00:02:16,511
<i>There is just you.</i>

13
00:02:18,221 --> 00:02:20,640
<i>You won't always have a primary surgeon,</i>

14
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:22,976
<i>an anesthesiologist,</i>

15
00:02:23,059 --> 00:02:25,687
<i>an assistant, an OR nurse,</i>

16
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:29,566
<i>or a scrub nurse</i>
<i>with you for every surgery.</i>

17
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:33,236
A doctor

18
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:38,491
must always stay by their patient's side.

19
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:42,704
That is our duty.

20
00:02:45,665 --> 00:02:46,708
It's why

21
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:50,003
we chose to practice this profession.

22
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:52,839
Don't stop. What else?

23
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:55,216
Auntie, keep talking.

24
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:57,051
Don't fall asleep.

25
00:03:01,389 --> 00:03:02,932
If the transplant fails,

26
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:06,603
it means there are three lives lost.

27
00:03:07,353 --> 00:03:09,147
The person who donated the heart,

28
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:12,400
the person receiving the heart,

29
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:14,485
and…

30
00:03:17,071 --> 00:03:19,032
the person who also…

31
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:21,618
needed that heart.

32
00:03:29,751 --> 00:03:32,754
Yeah. That's right.

33
00:03:36,216 --> 00:03:38,426
- Auntie!
- Focus!

34
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:51,731
To this patient,

35
00:03:52,815 --> 00:03:55,276
you are all they have right now.

36
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,237
And you mean everything to them.

37
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:01,574
That's what… a doctor is.

38
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:11,751
Focus.

39
00:04:12,877 --> 00:04:13,836
Right.

40
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:31,813
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

41
00:04:31,896 --> 00:04:32,855
EPISODE 10

42
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:36,276
Again, the yes votes
must exceed 80% in order to, um…

43
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:42,407
to pass the resolution.

44
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:44,701
I doubt they got the tumor out yet.

45
00:04:44,784 --> 00:04:49,414
Okay, voting will now begin.
Front row, please come up first.

46
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:03,011
- Um…
- Uh, I can't help it.

47
00:05:03,094 --> 00:05:05,847
This is the best I can do.

48
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:09,851
Can't-- Can't you go a little faster?

49
00:05:09,934 --> 00:05:10,893
I'll-- I'll try.

50
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:14,814
Metz.

51
00:05:15,815 --> 00:05:17,942
Please tie off the spot you're holding.

52
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:20,695
Huh? Oh, okay. Tie, tie, tie, tie.

53
00:05:20,778 --> 00:05:21,863
Right, tie.

54
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:24,949
Come on, faster, faster. Damn it…

55
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:25,867
TIME: 01:41 P.M.

56
00:05:26,909 --> 00:05:28,494
They must be voting now.

57
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,585
2:11 P.M.
SUNDAY, MAY 3

58
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:46,637
Hey, why are Director Bu and Dr. Bae
just sitting in their seats?

59
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:48,431
What's wrong with them?

60
00:05:59,859 --> 00:06:00,902
WAITING ROOM

61
00:06:02,487 --> 00:06:05,114
Mi-gyeong,
you think they're gonna make it?

62
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:10,078
I don't know, they've
really got their work cut out for them.

63
00:06:10,161 --> 00:06:12,747
I wish somebody would get in there
and lend them a hand.

64
00:06:22,298 --> 00:06:23,299
Uh…

65
00:06:25,343 --> 00:06:26,719
Sir, uh…

66
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:31,724
Director Bu. Dr. Bae.

67
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:34,310
Aren't you going to vote?

68
00:06:44,862 --> 00:06:47,073
Get up there. What are you waiting for?

69
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:10,847
ARE YOU IN FAVOR OF INTERNS AND RESIDENTS
SUBMITTING THEIR RESIGNATIONS?

70
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:13,516
Geez.

71
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:18,438
Hey, Director Bu.
Director Bu, not that way!

72
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:26,904
What the hell does he think he's doing?

73
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:31,284
- What's he up to?
- Today, at our hospital,

74
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:34,036
there is only one operating room

75
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,872
with a surgery in progress.

76
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:38,958
Operating Room 7.

77
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:42,128
At this moment, in our largest OR

78
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:45,882
a surgery is underway
on the smallest of children.

79
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:47,425
And that child

80
00:07:47,508 --> 00:07:51,345
is a patient who was repeatedly
turned away by our main hospital,

81
00:07:51,429 --> 00:07:55,057
as well as the surgical team here,
and many other hospitals.

82
00:07:55,766 --> 00:07:57,185
Today, that child

83
00:07:57,268 --> 00:08:00,521
is receiving the surgery
that no one else would perform.

84
00:08:01,647 --> 00:08:03,858
The procedure essentially entails

85
00:08:03,941 --> 00:08:05,776
removing six organs,

86
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:07,195
resecting the tumor,

87
00:08:07,278 --> 00:08:09,572
and placing the organs back into the body.

88
00:08:09,655 --> 00:08:15,036
It's called multivisceral ex vivo
tumor resection and autotransplantation.

89
00:08:17,079 --> 00:08:19,999
And that's a risky surgery.

90
00:08:21,375 --> 00:08:25,087
This is that child's last hope,
her last chance for survival.

91
00:08:27,423 --> 00:08:30,384
Everyone, if we are physicians,

92
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:32,386
if we are truly doctors of medicine,

93
00:08:34,096 --> 00:08:36,807
then my question is, where do we belong?

94
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:41,145
In this room, voting,

95
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:44,106
using the lives of
our patients as bargaining chips?

96
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:47,193
Or do we instead belong there…

97
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:49,737
in that operating room.

98
00:08:53,908 --> 00:08:55,660
This is the choice that I make.

99
00:09:02,708 --> 00:09:04,418
Tell me, have you lost your mind?

100
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:06,045
What are you waiting for? Go stop him.

101
00:09:07,129 --> 00:09:08,172
Now!

102
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:15,137
You know, that insanely
complicated surgery they're doing?

103
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:16,847
Gye Su-jeong's the surgeon.

104
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:19,517
And even though it's her,
she's bound to need extra hands.

105
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:20,476
So, Doctor, um…

106
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,853
You said your niece is seven,
right? That girl is eight.

107
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:25,314
The next time you see your niece,
you're gonna be so--

108
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:28,317
You're gonna feel terrible about yourself,
but I know what that's like, okay?

109
00:09:29,068 --> 00:09:31,737
Seong-gyu, let's go.

110
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:43,874
Hey, Dr. Bae.
Stop with the nonsense already.

111
00:09:44,542 --> 00:09:46,168
Go bring the director back.

112
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:48,296
And you, get on with it!

113
00:10:05,563 --> 00:10:11,402
All right, the voting has now ended.
We will now begin counting the…

114
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:18,159
What? Has everybody gone crazy?

115
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:20,911
So where is this OR 7?

116
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:25,916
Damn it.

117
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:28,961
Oh, geez.

118
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:33,174
Dr. Do, pick up the pace.
We're really tight on time.

119
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:36,677
Oh, I'm going as fast as I can.
That's the best I can do.

120
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:40,348
Oh, come on! I'm frustrated too, you know…

121
00:10:40,431 --> 00:10:43,017
- Let's focus.
- Okay.

122
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:46,020
I don't know…

123
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:48,731
Can we really pull this off,
just the three of us?

124
00:10:48,814 --> 00:10:51,567
If you've got time to ask that,
you should speed up.

125
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:55,279
Dr. Jo, try paging whoever's out there.

126
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:57,531
I get that they're afraid of
the repercussions,

127
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:59,283
but not even a single person shows up?

128
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:00,451
Unbelievable!

129
00:11:03,245 --> 00:11:04,830
Director! Dr. Bae!

130
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:07,333
Oh, we're saved! We're saved!

131
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:10,169
Hyeon-a, you're saved.

132
00:11:10,252 --> 00:11:11,796
I'm saved too!

133
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:13,464
Wow, you're twice as fast as I expected.

134
00:11:13,547 --> 00:11:15,549
We need to be three times faster.

135
00:11:16,425 --> 00:11:18,594
You really are something-- Who are you?

136
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:22,264
Hurry up and grab the harmonic.
Or use the Metzenbaum and tie it off.

137
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:25,101
- That voice…
- Ms. Jang?

138
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:27,144
Is that Director Jang Hui-suk?

139
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:29,480
Okay, stop talking now,
stop, stop, stop, stop!

140
00:11:29,563 --> 00:11:31,482
Come on, come on, come on.
Get over here and help!

141
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:35,528
Thank you, Director. Thank you so much!

142
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:37,279
Seriously, you guys are the best!

143
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,865
But Director, if you're here…

144
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:43,494
What about the vote?
You voted before you came, right? Right?

145
00:11:49,625 --> 00:11:53,170
The overwhelming result of 92% in favor

146
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:55,631
likely reflects the anxiety and suffering

147
00:11:55,715 --> 00:11:59,427
that young doctors have experienced
in this profession.

148
00:12:00,177 --> 00:12:03,639
If, due to this crisis, we are
unfairly persecuted by the government,

149
00:12:04,348 --> 00:12:07,226
we will unite, not just as colleagues
in the medical field,

150
00:12:07,309 --> 00:12:09,019
but as citizens of our country.

151
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:11,063
The reason we chose this profession

152
00:12:12,231 --> 00:12:13,899
was to help people in distress…

153
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:17,486
<i>Today, at our hospital,</i>

154
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:20,072
<i>there is only one operating room</i>

155
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,574
with a surgery in progress.

156
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:23,784
Operating Room 7.

157
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:26,579
At this moment, in our largest OR,

158
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:29,957
a surgery is underway
on the smallest of children.

159
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:33,753
…to cure patients

160
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:36,297
when disease and illness occur,

161
00:12:37,131 --> 00:12:42,094
and to contribute to the development
of healthcare in our country.

162
00:12:43,053 --> 00:12:44,054
Contributing to the--

163
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:46,098
- You did good. I got it now.
- Oh.

164
00:12:47,349 --> 00:12:48,350
All right!

165
00:12:49,226 --> 00:12:52,021
The current administration is determined

166
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:55,316
to see that this unjustified policy
is pushed through,

167
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:58,569
silencing anyone who dares to oppose,

168
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:02,239
abusing public authority to threaten us.

169
00:13:02,323 --> 00:13:04,909
Is this what
you people call communication?

170
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:11,207
<i>This is that child's last hope,</i>

171
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:12,875
<i>her last chance for survival.</i>

172
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:14,585
If we are physicians,

173
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:17,379
if we are truly doctors of medicine,

174
00:13:18,005 --> 00:13:20,841
then my question is, where do we belong?

175
00:13:20,925 --> 00:13:23,469
Seong-gyu, let's go.

176
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:27,807
Everyone,
let's show them our determination!

177
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:33,395
EXPANDING QUOTA
RUINS EDUCATION

178
00:13:39,693 --> 00:13:42,822
Gosh, why is it so hot?
It's so cold in here. Why am I hot?

179
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:45,449
- Should I wipe your sweat?
- No, no, no, not yet.

180
00:13:46,283 --> 00:13:48,994
Still, I think we're almost there.

181
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:05,594
Test, test. Can you hear me?
Director Bu! What's this?

182
00:14:05,678 --> 00:14:08,389
Dr. Do, I just thought
you went to the bathroom earlier.

183
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:10,516
You certainly do have guts, coming here.

184
00:14:10,599 --> 00:14:12,017
This is unacceptable.

185
00:14:12,101 --> 00:14:15,187
What do you think you're doing in here
instead of casting your votes?

186
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:17,898
I heard this surgery
isn't even approved by the IRB.

187
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:20,609
Are-Are all those things
I'm looking at right now--

188
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:23,654
Are those the patient's organs?
You all must be insane!

189
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:27,157
You are violating both the hospital's code
of ethics and the foundation's, as well.

190
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:29,201
Stop the surgery!

191
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:31,996
How is closing up a patient
halfway through surgery ethical?

192
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:35,791
Do you hear what I'm saying?
Stop the surgery!

193
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:40,963
Hyeon-a here
hasn't even been to school yet.

194
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:44,049
She's never given her mother a hard time.

195
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:47,469
But I hope Hyeon-a
becomes a really disobedient daughter.

196
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:51,307
So I will make sure

197
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:53,517
that Hyeon-a grows up to be an adult.

198
00:15:01,775 --> 00:15:03,235
We need to either go in there

199
00:15:03,319 --> 00:15:05,529
and drag them out,
or call private security to do it.

200
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:06,906
Just get it done.

201
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:09,325
Gu Bon-pyeong!

202
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:13,662
I am exercising my authority as director.

203
00:15:13,746 --> 00:15:17,082
This surgery will be carried through
to completion.

204
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:30,012
Director Bu Seung-gwon!

205
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:33,390
You just made a huge mistake--
No, you just committed a grave offense!

206
00:15:33,474 --> 00:15:36,852
How dare raise your voice like that to the
chairman of our foundation and Magnolia--

207
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:39,229
- You're in charge of one damn hospital!
- Let's do that thing you're so good at.

208
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:42,066
And now what?
You think you're untouchable?

209
00:15:42,149 --> 00:15:44,818
How dare you! You must be crazy!

210
00:15:44,902 --> 00:15:46,654
What--

211
00:15:58,165 --> 00:16:00,626
What's wrong? They turned off the mic?

212
00:16:00,709 --> 00:16:03,212
- Let's get out of here.
- That son of a-- Damn it! Geez.

213
00:16:24,483 --> 00:16:26,652
I'll just call in private security.

214
00:16:26,735 --> 00:16:29,113
You, give the management team a call.

215
00:16:29,905 --> 00:16:33,534
- There's a CCTV camera in there.
- What? What about it?

216
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:38,205
This is a pediatric surgery.
If you send private security in there

217
00:16:38,288 --> 00:16:40,708
and then they contaminate the OR
and stop the surgery,

218
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:42,084
and then footage of it gets out,

219
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:44,086
the popularity of
the strike will take a hit.

220
00:16:44,169 --> 00:16:45,921
Ugh, those damn
surveillance cameras, I swear…

221
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:48,841
In order to crush them,
we need a legitimate reason.

222
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:51,593
I'll teach them a very hard lesson.

223
00:16:52,386 --> 00:16:54,263
- Schedule a meeting.
- Yes, sir.

224
00:17:00,269 --> 00:17:02,521
Okay. Starting the reconstruction.

225
00:17:09,528 --> 00:17:10,446
Dr. Kim.

226
00:17:10,529 --> 00:17:12,197
I'm here. I know you've been waiting.

227
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:13,574
Ugh, geez.

228
00:17:13,657 --> 00:17:17,786
Everyone, I'm finally here, so… I…

229
00:17:21,373 --> 00:17:23,250
What do I need to do, Dr. Jo?

230
00:17:23,333 --> 00:17:25,627
I had a feeling you'd come,
so I texted you not to.

231
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:27,296
Wow, even Director Bu is here.

232
00:17:27,379 --> 00:17:30,007
Amazing. But who is that over there?

233
00:17:30,924 --> 00:17:32,634
Stop whispering and get moving already.

234
00:17:32,718 --> 00:17:34,595
We're about to put the organs back in.

235
00:17:34,678 --> 00:17:36,013
Okay, understood.

236
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:43,729
Reconstruction of the IVC
with a synthetic graft is complete.

237
00:17:43,812 --> 00:17:46,273
- Let's place the organs back in the body.
- Okay.

238
00:18:27,397 --> 00:18:31,068
Oh, please. Let the surgery be successful.

239
00:18:31,944 --> 00:18:33,654
Just please save that little girl.

240
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:35,364
OPERATION TIME, TIME, ANESTHESIA TIME

241
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:38,742
We'll remove the clamps now.

242
00:18:39,409 --> 00:18:40,744
Is the saline ready?

243
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:43,122
- Yes.
- Removing the clamps.

244
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:59,847
Keep going. You need to do this well.

245
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:01,890
- Okay, will do.
- There's no bleeding.

246
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:04,101
Looks like the sutures were done nicely.

247
00:19:04,184 --> 00:19:07,146
This is part is always
so nerve-racking for me.

248
00:19:07,229 --> 00:19:10,899
Right? If the organs don't
pink up, it means they're damaged.

249
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:13,360
Then everything we've done so far,

250
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:15,821
along with all of Hyeon-a's organs…

251
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:17,364
Will go to waste.

252
00:19:22,369 --> 00:19:25,622
It looks--
Why is it like this? Why is it that color?

253
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:30,085
Damn it. Is it just me,
or is the color still not returning?

254
00:19:30,169 --> 00:19:32,462
Again.
Prepare more saline. Make it warmer.

255
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:35,674
- Ah, okay.
- Oh, Hyeon-a, come on!

256
00:19:35,757 --> 00:19:37,634
Check for blood clots with the ultrasound.

257
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:39,469
- Okay.
- Ooh, ooh, ooh! It's coming!

258
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:42,764
It's coming! The color's coming back!
Look! The color, the color!

259
00:19:52,608 --> 00:19:53,567
BP?

260
00:19:55,694 --> 00:19:58,363
- Blood pressure holding steady.
- Turn off the shunt.

261
00:19:58,447 --> 00:20:00,616
Oh! I'll do it. I will, I will. I will.

262
00:20:39,696 --> 00:20:40,864
Seeing her like this…

263
00:20:40,948 --> 00:20:43,659
My goodness… She's small.

264
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:45,994
So small…

265
00:20:46,662 --> 00:20:48,497
She really is so small.

266
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:50,958
Oh, Hyeon-a.

267
00:20:52,084 --> 00:20:55,837
Oh, Hyeon-a, y-you did so, so well.

268
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:04,304
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

269
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:08,058
The surgery is over.

270
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:14,314
- Good-- Good job.
- Thank goodness.

271
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:27,828
Good job, good job.

272
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:31,415
Everyone…

273
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:34,459
- Thank you.
- Whoa, what are you doing?

274
00:21:34,543 --> 00:21:36,211
Don't bow. Don't bow. Don't do that.

275
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:40,090
We all ended up here because you bowed.

276
00:21:41,091 --> 00:21:43,135
Stop acting so out of character.

277
00:21:43,218 --> 00:21:46,138
Just do what you usually do and leave.

278
00:22:56,541 --> 00:22:58,835
So?

279
00:23:11,264 --> 00:23:12,432
Go on.

280
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:27,322
Thank you, thank you.
From the bottom of my heart.

281
00:23:30,409 --> 00:23:32,494
Thank you for saving her, Doctor.

282
00:23:44,464 --> 00:23:45,507
Good work.

283
00:23:51,012 --> 00:23:54,349
Why is she so awkward?

284
00:23:55,767 --> 00:23:56,893
It is awkward.

285
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:59,396
She never expects to
get thanked, you know?

286
00:23:59,479 --> 00:24:01,773
Mmm. That's true.

287
00:24:02,524 --> 00:24:03,984
That's our Gye Su-jeong.

288
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:18,206
Ow! Ow, wait a minute.

289
00:24:18,290 --> 00:24:22,169
Ugh, oh, hold on.
Oh, my, my leg, I got-- I got a cramp.

290
00:24:22,252 --> 00:24:24,379
- Ow.
- Dr. Kim, just now,

291
00:24:25,380 --> 00:24:29,426
you just betrayed all the medical science
we've been practicing up to now.

292
00:24:30,343 --> 00:24:32,429
Hey, it's habit, a habit.

293
00:24:32,512 --> 00:24:34,806
Hey, we've all had
that-- that extraordinary experience

294
00:24:34,890 --> 00:24:36,933
when our grandmothers used a needle
to prick our fingers

295
00:24:37,017 --> 00:24:39,019
and cure our-- ow, our stomach ache--
Ow, it's back.

296
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:42,814
Boy you made such a fuss
when you blew in at the last minute.

297
00:24:42,898 --> 00:24:44,691
Well, it's because
I haven't done surgery in a while.

298
00:24:44,774 --> 00:24:46,443
Wait a sec, look who's talking.

299
00:24:46,526 --> 00:24:48,236
You showed up late, too.

300
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:50,906
I was there from the start, slowpoke!

301
00:24:56,870 --> 00:24:59,539
Wow! Wow, I knew it!

302
00:24:59,623 --> 00:25:01,917
Ms. Jang and I are on
the exact same wavelength.

303
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,126
Okay, everyone, let's go.

304
00:25:03,210 --> 00:25:04,461
What do you mean, go where?

305
00:25:04,544 --> 00:25:07,130
- To the team dinner.
- What dinner?

306
00:25:07,214 --> 00:25:09,966
Since everyone worked so hard,
Ms. Jang said she and Dr. Gye

307
00:25:10,050 --> 00:25:12,219
are gonna treat us all to dinner!

308
00:25:12,302 --> 00:25:13,595
- Whoa, whoa!
- Let's go.

309
00:25:13,678 --> 00:25:15,514
- What a nice surprise.
- A surprise indeed.

310
00:25:15,597 --> 00:25:16,848
- All right.
- Wow.

311
00:25:16,932 --> 00:25:17,807
Looks great!

312
00:25:17,891 --> 00:25:19,768
- Here, why don't you take this.
- Thank you.

313
00:25:19,851 --> 00:25:21,603
Eung-gu,
some pickled radish over here too.

314
00:25:21,686 --> 00:25:22,521
Got it.

315
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:23,688
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

316
00:25:23,772 --> 00:25:25,690
- Here's some pickled radish.
- Here, for you.

317
00:25:25,774 --> 00:25:29,110
- Pickled radish for you. Enjoy, enjoy.
- Oh, thank you.

318
00:25:31,446 --> 00:25:34,699
Uh, everyone, because of the strike

319
00:25:34,783 --> 00:25:37,452
all the nicer restaurants
near the hospital closed early.

320
00:25:38,245 --> 00:25:40,038
This was the closest place
that was still open.

321
00:25:40,121 --> 00:25:41,957
There was a barbecue restaurant open
on the way here.

322
00:25:42,040 --> 00:25:43,625
There were a couple, I think.

323
00:25:43,708 --> 00:25:46,795
Ah, so I decided, to make up for it,

324
00:25:46,878 --> 00:25:49,881
I ordered number 1 through 25,
their entire menu.

325
00:25:49,965 --> 00:25:53,385
So, just sit back,
relax and enjoy the food.

326
00:25:53,468 --> 00:25:56,054
You know, everybody
did a wonderful job today.

327
00:25:56,137 --> 00:25:58,098
- Great work.
- Good work, everyone.

328
00:25:58,181 --> 00:26:00,016
- Good work, everyone.
- Everyone was amazing.

329
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:04,479
Ah! Oh, and you should all make sure
to grab one of my cards before you go.

330
00:26:04,563 --> 00:26:06,731
Okay, cheers!

331
00:26:06,815 --> 00:26:09,192
- Cheers! Great work, everyone!
- Cheers.

332
00:26:09,276 --> 00:26:10,986
- Good job.
- Great work.

333
00:26:11,069 --> 00:26:12,654
- Great job.
- Great work.

334
00:26:12,737 --> 00:26:14,114
- Cheers.
- Really great work, everyone.

335
00:26:14,197 --> 00:26:15,115
- Here's to you!
- Cheers!

336
00:26:15,198 --> 00:26:16,491
- Great work!
- Thanks.

337
00:26:17,242 --> 00:26:18,743
- This is so nice.
- A toast.

338
00:26:18,827 --> 00:26:21,121
I just wanna say that today, as a doctor,

339
00:26:21,204 --> 00:26:22,289
I was…

340
00:26:23,123 --> 00:26:24,374
I was so genuinely moved--

341
00:26:24,457 --> 00:26:27,252
- Thanks for the food.
- Thank you for the food.

342
00:26:27,335 --> 00:26:29,129
Thank you for the food.

343
00:26:29,212 --> 00:26:31,339
Whoa, Dr. Gye, take your time,

344
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:33,091
Nobody's going to take it away from you.

345
00:26:34,175 --> 00:26:35,010
Mmm.

346
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:36,720
Oh.

347
00:26:37,679 --> 00:26:40,223
Is this place open 24 hours?

348
00:26:40,307 --> 00:26:42,767
Why? You planning to eat
for 24 hours straight?

349
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:45,812
So you can eat when you wake up
and again when you go to sleep?

350
00:26:45,895 --> 00:26:48,064
That's the answer
you'd expect from Dr. Gye.

351
00:26:51,401 --> 00:26:52,444
Delicious.

352
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:57,115
They say there's no paradise to escape to,
but look what they call this place:

353
00:26:57,198 --> 00:26:58,408
"Gimbap Paradise."

354
00:26:58,491 --> 00:26:59,576
GIMBAP PARADISE

355
00:26:59,659 --> 00:27:01,244
It sure is paradise for Gye Su-jeong.

356
00:27:03,371 --> 00:27:04,873
It's good. Everything's good.

357
00:27:12,672 --> 00:27:16,009
- It's good.
- Director, you eat this?

358
00:27:16,092 --> 00:27:18,928
It's been a while, but I like it.
Eat up, both of you.

359
00:27:19,012 --> 00:27:20,930
Sure, okay.

360
00:27:22,766 --> 00:27:24,184
It sure has been a long time

361
00:27:24,267 --> 00:27:27,729
since we've shared a meal like this
after a long day's work.

362
00:27:28,313 --> 00:27:31,274
- Let's eat.
- Yeah! Let's eat!

363
00:27:32,942 --> 00:27:35,278
Oh! Oh, thank you.

364
00:27:38,990 --> 00:27:39,949
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

365
00:27:41,618 --> 00:27:44,496
Today in the OR,
you did a really good job.

366
00:27:54,964 --> 00:27:55,799
Thank you.

367
00:27:57,467 --> 00:28:00,261
Wow, Dr. Gye, you can
actually say things like that now?

368
00:28:02,222 --> 00:28:04,140
To all you doctors, and Ms. Jang…

369
00:28:05,809 --> 00:28:07,560
When you showed up today to help,

370
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:08,770
I was really…

371
00:28:08,853 --> 00:28:10,438
I just, I was really…

372
00:28:11,022 --> 00:28:12,065
I was…

373
00:28:12,148 --> 00:28:15,485
it just-- it meant a lot to me,
so thank you, really. Oh.

374
00:28:15,568 --> 00:28:17,153
Did you get drunk on yogurt?

375
00:28:17,237 --> 00:28:20,532
I think our team dinner should've been at
a different type of restaurant, actually.

376
00:28:20,615 --> 00:28:22,158
- Uh, but since we're here…
- Ah! Hey!

377
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:23,743
- …I'm gonna start with that <i>rabokki.</i>
- Mmm!

378
00:28:24,577 --> 00:28:26,996
Mmm! Mmm!

379
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:30,166
It's true, food always tastes better
after a hard day's work.

380
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:31,084
Put that down.

381
00:28:31,167 --> 00:28:33,169
- I've been eyeing it for a while now.
- Dr. Gye wants…

382
00:28:33,253 --> 00:28:35,255
Eat the <i>jjolbokki.</i>
It's basically the same thing.

383
00:28:35,338 --> 00:28:37,841
- Hey, this is for Dr. Gye--
- Hey, hey, hey. Director Bu wants some.

384
00:28:37,924 --> 00:28:40,385
- Dr. Gye gets some first.
- Ah, you caught me.

385
00:28:40,468 --> 00:28:42,262
I'm having the <i>donkkaseu.</i>

386
00:28:42,345 --> 00:28:44,973
Ah, Dr. Bae, could
you pass me the dumplings over there?

387
00:28:45,056 --> 00:28:47,142
- I want more of that.
- Thank you.

388
00:28:47,225 --> 00:28:48,143
Oh, geez.

389
00:28:48,226 --> 00:28:49,644
- This is good.
- Yeah, it's really good.

390
00:28:49,728 --> 00:28:51,354
Drink some water while you're eating,

391
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:52,856
or you'll get indigestion.

392
00:28:52,939 --> 00:28:55,150
- Mmm! This is good.
- This sauce is excellent.

393
00:28:55,859 --> 00:28:57,986
- Eat slowly. Slowly.
- Hui-suk, you're crying?

394
00:28:58,069 --> 00:29:00,488
- Oh, then, Dr. Bae, could you--
- Don't be silly.

395
00:29:00,572 --> 00:29:03,408
It looks like Su-jeong's
made some friends, huh?

396
00:29:03,491 --> 00:29:05,368
There are both meat
and kimchi fried dumplings.

397
00:29:05,452 --> 00:29:07,120
Nah, just workmates, that's all.

398
00:29:08,037 --> 00:29:10,415
But at least she's not lonely.
That's pretty nice.

399
00:29:13,501 --> 00:29:15,503
- I want some more of that.
- It is nice.

400
00:29:15,587 --> 00:29:16,421
Better slow down.

401
00:29:16,504 --> 00:29:18,381
- Do you want any more? It's almost gone.
- Go ahead, it's yours.

402
00:29:18,465 --> 00:29:19,799
These are the best ones here.

403
00:29:19,883 --> 00:29:21,509
How do they compare
to what we have at home?

404
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:23,636
Want us to show you?
All right, watch this.

405
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:26,055
- Oh, seriously? What are you guys doing?
- Look. Okay, here we go.

406
00:29:26,139 --> 00:29:28,391
- Yeah, go ahead.
- Okay. One, two… Hey, hey!

407
00:29:34,522 --> 00:29:36,024
Whoa!

408
00:29:36,107 --> 00:29:38,526
You are good at that!

409
00:29:38,610 --> 00:29:40,820
- Wow!
- Can I try throwing one too?

410
00:29:40,904 --> 00:29:42,197
- Sure you can.
- Really?

411
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:44,282
- Of course.
- Then how about a dumpling?

412
00:29:44,365 --> 00:29:46,201
- A dumpling? Can do.
- Do it! Let's see it.

413
00:29:46,284 --> 00:29:48,620
- A dumpling? Totally.
- Let me just try throwing this.

414
00:29:48,703 --> 00:29:50,872
Okay, one, two, three.

415
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:56,085
See? Told you.

416
00:29:56,169 --> 00:29:59,005
Let's set her down there. Oh, man.

417
00:29:59,088 --> 00:30:00,131
- Okay, okay, okay.
- Careful.

418
00:30:00,215 --> 00:30:01,549
- She's fast asleep.
- My goodness.

419
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:02,717
- Oh dear, whoa.
- Are you okay?

420
00:30:02,801 --> 00:30:06,054
- Ms. Jang.
- Huh? I'm fine, I'm fine. Ow, my back.

421
00:30:06,137 --> 00:30:08,556
- Just lean back.
- When did she get so heavy?

422
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,641
Eung-gu.

423
00:30:09,724 --> 00:30:12,185
When the bus gets here,
you should carry her on, okay?

424
00:30:16,439 --> 00:30:18,483
Aw, really?

425
00:30:18,566 --> 00:30:21,277
Earlier today at the hospital,
I did so much knitting,

426
00:30:21,361 --> 00:30:23,029
I feel like my eyes are gonna pop out.

427
00:30:23,112 --> 00:30:25,114
- My back feels like it's about to snap--
- Oh, for crying out loud.

428
00:30:25,198 --> 00:30:28,159
- I can carry her.
- Oh, no, no. Don't do that. It's fine.

429
00:30:28,243 --> 00:30:30,954
I'm pretty sure she hasn't gotten
any sleep at all for the past few days.

430
00:30:31,037 --> 00:30:34,207
She was too busy
thinking about the surgery, I bet.

431
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:38,461
You always look out for her. We want
you to know that we're really grateful.

432
00:30:38,545 --> 00:30:42,298
Oh, no, gosh, not at all.
I'm the one who's grateful.

433
00:30:42,382 --> 00:30:43,842
Oh, this works out well.

434
00:30:43,925 --> 00:30:44,801
Huh?

435
00:30:44,884 --> 00:30:46,845
Your bus arrives
earlier than ours, Dr. Park.

436
00:30:46,928 --> 00:30:50,139
Oh. Only…
I should see you off before I go.

437
00:30:50,223 --> 00:30:51,307
Oh, there's no need.

438
00:30:51,391 --> 00:30:54,269
There are four of us here,
but you're by yourself.

439
00:30:54,936 --> 00:30:56,646
We don't want to abandon you here.

440
00:30:56,729 --> 00:31:00,066
Being by yourself
at a bus stop feels so lonely.

441
00:31:01,192 --> 00:31:02,652
Oh… Shh.

442
00:31:04,612 --> 00:31:07,115
Oh, I was curious, Ms. Jang.

443
00:31:07,198 --> 00:31:10,869
How did you end up teaching
and taking care of your niece?

444
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:19,210
Well, to tell the truth,
we're not actually related.

445
00:31:19,294 --> 00:31:22,422
Oh, wait. You're not?

446
00:31:22,505 --> 00:31:25,884
Oh, but… how did you…

447
00:31:27,927 --> 00:31:31,639
She's the daughter of my best friend.

448
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:33,933
She passed away,

449
00:31:34,017 --> 00:31:35,476
so I took in Su-jeong.

450
00:31:36,394 --> 00:31:39,856
And it turns out,
she ended up being my savior, you know?

451
00:31:41,107 --> 00:31:42,901
She accepted me like I was family.

452
00:31:46,696 --> 00:31:49,407
Su-jeong is the only family
I've got, actually.

453
00:31:50,366 --> 00:31:53,077
- I mean, that we've got.
- Mmm!

454
00:31:58,166 --> 00:31:59,834
Sounds a lot like my family story.

455
00:32:01,210 --> 00:32:02,670
- Hmm?
- Hmm?

456
00:32:03,338 --> 00:32:06,591
Oh, uh… So you're saying…

457
00:32:08,051 --> 00:32:10,511
Uh, my parents told me

458
00:32:10,595 --> 00:32:13,014
they saw me at an orphanage
they volunteered at,

459
00:32:13,097 --> 00:32:15,475
and I would always
sit quietly in the corner,

460
00:32:15,558 --> 00:32:17,477
just sitting, never smiling or crying.

461
00:32:18,519 --> 00:32:22,148
They said every time they went home, they
would cry, because it broke their hearts.

462
00:32:22,231 --> 00:32:26,694
But I don't remember any of it.
I was like, "Was I really doing that?"

463
00:32:28,863 --> 00:32:30,782
And apparently, all they could think was,

464
00:32:30,865 --> 00:32:33,534
"Let's take him home and try to
make him smile as much as we can."

465
00:32:34,452 --> 00:32:36,537
It's true, you wanna
do things for your kids,

466
00:32:36,621 --> 00:32:40,583
dress them in warm clothes,
give them a warm bed to sleep in,

467
00:32:41,334 --> 00:32:43,795
and fill them up with warm food.

468
00:32:43,878 --> 00:32:45,546
Yeah.

469
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:47,173
All moms and dads feel the way you do.

470
00:32:51,886 --> 00:32:53,429
It's a wonderful thing…

471
00:32:54,764 --> 00:32:55,890
family.

472
00:32:59,060 --> 00:33:01,270
Yeah, when I suddenly ended up in one,

473
00:33:02,397 --> 00:33:03,815
I found that out.

474
00:33:07,527 --> 00:33:10,822
Dr. Park,
thank you for all your hard work today.

475
00:33:10,905 --> 00:33:12,782
Oh, gosh, no, thank you.

476
00:33:13,574 --> 00:33:14,909
Um…

477
00:33:16,119 --> 00:33:17,120
You know,

478
00:33:17,954 --> 00:33:20,373
today was a day
I don't think I'll ever forget.

479
00:33:21,499 --> 00:33:22,834
That's 'cause, today…

480
00:33:24,293 --> 00:33:26,754
I really felt like I was an actual doctor.

481
00:33:29,757 --> 00:33:32,176
<i>The 3:20 bus will be arriving shortly.</i>

482
00:33:32,260 --> 00:33:35,054
- Oh. Okay, I guess I'll see you later.
- Ah, okay.

483
00:33:35,138 --> 00:33:36,848
- Ah, little doctor.
- Get home safely.

484
00:33:36,931 --> 00:33:38,683
- Goodbye, have a good night.
- Have a safe trip home.

485
00:33:38,766 --> 00:33:39,976
- Bye.
- Mmm.

486
00:33:41,102 --> 00:33:43,896
He's leaving. Hey, no.
Over here, this way. There, there.

487
00:33:43,980 --> 00:33:45,023
Yeah.

488
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:07,754
Let's see who texted.

489
00:34:09,714 --> 00:34:11,549
DAD
MOM

490
00:34:11,632 --> 00:34:13,384
MOM: ARE YOU STILL AT THE HOSPITAL?

491
00:34:13,468 --> 00:34:15,470
<i>Son, you must be so busy.</i>

492
00:34:15,553 --> 00:34:18,222
<i>I haven't heard from you</i>
<i>in a while. I'm a little worried.</i>

493
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:19,932
<i>You're not skipping any meals, are you?</i>

494
00:34:20,016 --> 00:34:22,518
<i>Pretty soon, I'll forget</i>
<i>what your voice sounds like.</i>

495
00:34:25,271 --> 00:34:26,355
DAD

496
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:28,858
<i>Mom's worried because</i>
<i>you're not answering your phone.</i>

497
00:34:28,941 --> 00:34:30,651
<i>I told her not to call you too often,</i>

498
00:34:30,735 --> 00:34:32,737
<i>since it's tough studying</i>
<i>to become a doctor.</i>

499
00:34:32,820 --> 00:34:34,197
<i>You're not sick, are you?</i>

500
00:34:35,531 --> 00:34:38,534
<i>I'm fine.</i>
<i>I'll make sure to give Mom a call.</i>

501
00:34:54,801 --> 00:34:58,679
ONYU NURSING HOME

502
00:35:11,692 --> 00:35:13,236
Round two, just us!

503
00:35:13,319 --> 00:35:14,904
- Sounds good!
- Here you go.

504
00:35:18,449 --> 00:35:19,575
All right.

505
00:35:20,451 --> 00:35:22,078
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

506
00:35:32,046 --> 00:35:33,297
You know, today…

507
00:35:34,257 --> 00:35:35,508
could possibly have been

508
00:35:35,591 --> 00:35:37,260
- Director Bu's last surgery.
- Oh?

509
00:35:37,343 --> 00:35:39,554
He says he's losing his central vision.

510
00:35:40,388 --> 00:35:42,140
Ah…

511
00:35:51,023 --> 00:35:52,775
What's going on? Are you crying?

512
00:35:52,859 --> 00:35:55,945
No, it's not like I'm bawling or, uh…

513
00:35:57,738 --> 00:35:58,865
It's just…

514
00:36:00,908 --> 00:36:03,995
It was all so dreamlike today.

515
00:36:05,496 --> 00:36:10,168
I'm a doctor by profession, but was
I ever truly a doctor? I wasn't really.

516
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:20,636
<i>But… today,</i>

517
00:36:21,554 --> 00:36:22,930
<i>I saved someone.</i>

518
00:36:34,775 --> 00:36:36,861
<i>I saved a child's life.</i>

519
00:36:39,947 --> 00:36:42,074
You save lives every day.

520
00:36:42,742 --> 00:36:43,868
It's our job.

521
00:36:44,660 --> 00:36:45,995
That's true.

522
00:36:46,787 --> 00:36:48,289
That's true.

523
00:36:48,372 --> 00:36:49,290
I, um…

524
00:36:50,499 --> 00:36:52,877
I guess I just don't think
that way very often.

525
00:36:54,795 --> 00:36:56,881
But that's what being a doctor really is.

526
00:36:57,590 --> 00:36:58,507
It's such a…

527
00:36:59,383 --> 00:37:00,343
weight.

528
00:37:01,177 --> 00:37:02,303
Or maybe…

529
00:37:02,386 --> 00:37:04,222
I just avoid thinking that way.

530
00:37:05,806 --> 00:37:08,559
Since I'm no good at it. Damn it…

531
00:37:09,143 --> 00:37:12,230
Aw, snap out of it. You have
one sip of beer and you get like this?

532
00:37:24,242 --> 00:37:25,493
<i>Today,</i>

533
00:37:26,452 --> 00:37:27,536
I was a doctor.

534
00:37:29,163 --> 00:37:30,414
Yes.

535
00:37:37,588 --> 00:37:41,300
- What? Me crying is funny?
- No, no. It's not that.

536
00:37:41,384 --> 00:37:43,761
It's Director Bu, what he did earlier.

537
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:46,681
"Gu Bon-pyeong!"

538
00:37:49,767 --> 00:37:52,311
I felt like he was
going to explode with joy.

539
00:37:54,230 --> 00:37:57,608
And Kim Chang-su's face? Did you see it?
I hate that guy even more.

540
00:37:58,192 --> 00:38:01,028
I forgot that there's a tomorrow.

541
00:38:03,698 --> 00:38:05,366
You're finally realizing
the trouble you've caused?

542
00:38:05,449 --> 00:38:07,952
Uh-huh.
I really think Director Bu's lost it.

543
00:38:09,870 --> 00:38:12,373
- I think now I'm gonna lose it too.
- Go ahead, lose it.

544
00:38:14,834 --> 00:38:16,877
I think we all did that today, don't you?

545
00:38:19,046 --> 00:38:22,508
Oh, well.
Still, tomorrow won't be like yesterday.

546
00:38:24,510 --> 00:38:26,762
And after everything
I've gone through today,

547
00:38:26,846 --> 00:38:28,931
I don't want to go back to yesterday.

548
00:38:31,183 --> 00:38:33,602
Oh, geez. What was I thinking?

549
00:38:33,686 --> 00:38:35,479
I swear.

550
00:38:35,563 --> 00:38:36,939
Oh, man.

551
00:38:44,530 --> 00:38:47,366
I LOVE YOU, UNCLE

552
00:39:05,259 --> 00:39:06,260
She's grown.

553
00:39:07,678 --> 00:39:09,305
She's still pretty small, though.

554
00:39:10,473 --> 00:39:11,807
Why are you so little?

555
00:39:14,518 --> 00:39:17,104
<i>You said your niece is seven,</i>
<i>right? That girl is eight.</i>

556
00:39:17,188 --> 00:39:19,482
The next time you see your niece,
you're gonna be so--

557
00:39:19,565 --> 00:39:21,942
you're gonna feel terrible about yourself,
and I know what that's like.

558
00:39:22,026 --> 00:39:24,737
<i>Okay? Seong-gyu, let's go.</i>

559
00:39:27,615 --> 00:39:29,033
Oh, geez…

560
00:39:31,327 --> 00:39:32,411
He was right.

561
00:39:43,172 --> 00:39:44,882
<i>Dr. Bae, the surgery…</i>

562
00:39:44,965 --> 00:39:45,800
DR. BAE HEUNG-GON

563
00:39:50,721 --> 00:39:52,598
<i>Dr. Bae, I'm sorry about earlier…</i>

564
00:39:55,643 --> 00:39:58,104
<i>Dr. Bae, how's the child…</i>

565
00:40:02,900 --> 00:40:04,402
<i>The surgery went well.</i>

566
00:40:04,944 --> 00:40:06,862
<i>The child now has a fighting chance.</i>

567
00:40:08,114 --> 00:40:11,492
<i>Seong-gyu, take care of yourself.</i>

568
00:40:35,057 --> 00:40:36,642
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

569
00:40:36,725 --> 00:40:39,728
It's weird. It's weird.

570
00:40:39,812 --> 00:40:42,606
What's going on? Why's it so quiet?

571
00:40:42,690 --> 00:40:44,442
So I'm not the only one
who feels that way?

572
00:40:44,525 --> 00:40:46,819
Hmm. You didn't startle me at all.

573
00:40:46,902 --> 00:40:49,321
- I was expecting you down here.
- Feels strange, huh?

574
00:40:49,405 --> 00:40:51,866
It's empty out front
for the first time in ages.

575
00:40:52,533 --> 00:40:54,034
There's no reporters,

576
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:56,537
no patients, no doctors.

577
00:40:57,705 --> 00:40:59,290
It happens every once in a while,

578
00:40:59,373 --> 00:41:01,250
but we're comparing it to yesterday.

579
00:41:01,333 --> 00:41:03,335
So it feels extra peaceful today.

580
00:41:16,932 --> 00:41:17,766
Wha--

581
00:41:18,642 --> 00:41:19,768
Hmm?

582
00:41:19,852 --> 00:41:21,520
PERSONNEL CHANGES

583
00:41:21,604 --> 00:41:22,605
SUSPENSION FROM DUTIES

584
00:41:22,688 --> 00:41:26,775
BU SEUNG-GWON, DO YUN-SIK, BAE HEUNG-GON,
JO WON-JIN, KIM SEONG-JIN, PARK TAE-GYEONG

585
00:41:30,029 --> 00:41:32,239
CONTRACT TERMINATION
GENERAL SURGERY, GYE SU-JEONG

586
00:41:34,533 --> 00:41:35,743
Oh, no…

587
00:41:43,042 --> 00:41:46,921
So even though they wouldn't respond to
multiple requests for approval, suddenly

588
00:41:47,004 --> 00:41:49,757
yesterday's surgery is going
to be subject to review by the IRB?

589
00:41:50,549 --> 00:41:52,468
And until that happens,

590
00:41:52,551 --> 00:41:53,802
we're all suspended?

591
00:41:54,345 --> 00:41:58,057
You know that carrying out a surgical
method that has yet to be authorized,

592
00:41:58,140 --> 00:42:01,894
even if it's urgent, prompts a mandatory
retrospective surgical review.

593
00:42:03,270 --> 00:42:05,731
I only mentioned it
because usually suspensions are issued

594
00:42:05,814 --> 00:42:07,107
after the review is complete.

595
00:42:07,191 --> 00:42:10,027
The purpose of this meeting
is to punish us, that's all.

596
00:42:10,110 --> 00:42:11,487
Okay, but then,

597
00:42:12,571 --> 00:42:14,657
why did you do that yesterday?

598
00:42:14,740 --> 00:42:16,909
Director, I'm asking you, why…

599
00:42:16,992 --> 00:42:22,414
If I'm being suspended, that means
I have to vacate this office too, right?

600
00:42:25,167 --> 00:42:28,295
Well, the meeting's scheduled
for this evening.

601
00:42:28,379 --> 00:42:32,550
Until then, you should try to persuade
the chairman and the members of Magnolia--

602
00:42:32,633 --> 00:42:34,093
We know who the internal members will be,

603
00:42:34,176 --> 00:42:35,761
but there'll be
outside members there, too.

604
00:42:35,844 --> 00:42:37,805
Specialists and such. Who are they?

605
00:42:39,723 --> 00:42:43,602
The external medical expert
is Mr. Kim Chang-su,

606
00:42:43,686 --> 00:42:47,106
and the patient representative is
Chairman Park Gwang-cheol,

607
00:42:47,189 --> 00:42:48,399
I believe.

608
00:42:48,482 --> 00:42:49,733
I mean,

609
00:42:49,817 --> 00:42:53,487
doesn't having a direct conflict
of interest automatically exclude you?

610
00:42:53,571 --> 00:42:56,240
The expert in legal issues
will be Attorney Won Ju-pil.

611
00:42:56,323 --> 00:42:57,199
Oh…

612
00:42:57,950 --> 00:42:58,993
Is he someone you know?

613
00:43:01,620 --> 00:43:04,665
He's the lawyer for Magnolia.

614
00:43:13,090 --> 00:43:14,425
Thanks for the pizza.

615
00:43:19,138 --> 00:43:22,516
Mmm! Am I a total glutton
for thinking this is delicious,

616
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:24,727
- despite what's going on?
- Mm-mmm. No, that'd be her.

617
00:43:24,810 --> 00:43:27,730
Hey, excuse me.
Aren't you gonna expound on the flavors?

618
00:43:27,813 --> 00:43:30,024
Makes the host feel good
about what they're serving. Watch.

619
00:43:31,483 --> 00:43:36,155
"Mmm! Mmm! The basil's essence
is exploding in my mouth right now!"

620
00:43:36,238 --> 00:43:39,950
"Pizza never fails. Dr. Kim Seong-jin,
you're the best ever."

621
00:43:40,034 --> 00:43:41,910
Would that be so hard
for you to do, Dr. Gye?

622
00:43:43,287 --> 00:43:45,539
Dr. Kim Seong-jin, you're the best ever.

623
00:43:49,293 --> 00:43:52,713
I texted you not to come because
there were so many doctors in the OR!

624
00:43:52,796 --> 00:43:54,632
Why did you insist on coming?

625
00:43:54,715 --> 00:43:57,134
You didn't do anything
and now you're facing disciplinary action.

626
00:43:57,801 --> 00:44:00,471
You got involved
for no reason at the last--

627
00:44:00,554 --> 00:44:02,264
Mmm, this one tastes good.

628
00:44:03,349 --> 00:44:04,516
How did you know?

629
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:06,810
Before the theater club,
I was in the samulnori club,

630
00:44:06,894 --> 00:44:07,728
the barrel drum guy,

631
00:44:07,811 --> 00:44:09,980
so be sure to call if you need someone
to beat the drums and raise hell,

632
00:44:10,064 --> 00:44:10,898
or I'll feel left out.

633
00:44:10,981 --> 00:44:13,567
Hey, why'd you say I didn't do much, huh?

634
00:44:13,651 --> 00:44:15,444
I helped out a lot in there.

635
00:44:15,527 --> 00:44:18,155
They kept using the strike as an excuse,

636
00:44:18,238 --> 00:44:20,199
'cause they didn't wanna
approve the surgery.

637
00:44:21,408 --> 00:44:24,036
Even so, we submitted
all the materials we compiled,

638
00:44:24,119 --> 00:44:25,704
so we'll be okay, right?

639
00:44:26,372 --> 00:44:29,708
I think that's very unlikely.
Did you tell Ms. Jang?

640
00:44:31,001 --> 00:44:33,629
- Yep.
- Mm-hmm, I bet she was furious.

641
00:44:34,546 --> 00:44:36,215
"I got fired. The IRB is meeting."

642
00:44:38,717 --> 00:44:41,929
"All right. See you later. Just you wait."

643
00:44:42,012 --> 00:44:43,180
Uh…

644
00:44:44,014 --> 00:44:45,599
That's even scarier.

645
00:44:47,309 --> 00:44:48,602
So if I'm fired,

646
00:44:49,561 --> 00:44:51,230
don't I get to go home for the day?

647
00:44:51,313 --> 00:44:54,441
Can you go play your drum
and raise hell right in her ear?

648
00:44:55,067 --> 00:44:57,611
You know, yesterday was
the first time I saw Dr. Gye do surgery.

649
00:44:57,695 --> 00:44:58,696
And she was so amazing

650
00:44:58,779 --> 00:45:01,615
that I didn't recognize her
and I almost introduced myself.

651
00:45:01,699 --> 00:45:04,576
But it looks like whoever that was
is still in the OR.

652
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:06,161
I wonder what they'll do.

653
00:45:07,955 --> 00:45:10,499
Well, since all of us there
just wanted to save the patient,

654
00:45:10,582 --> 00:45:12,167
I'm sure they'll rise to the occasion,

655
00:45:12,251 --> 00:45:13,210
as doctors and adults.

656
00:45:14,169 --> 00:45:16,463
Well, I'll take whatever consequences
come my way.

657
00:45:16,547 --> 00:45:18,716
If that little girl's gonna be okay,
nothing else matters.

658
00:45:19,675 --> 00:45:22,553
Her family could sue us
depending on the IRB results.

659
00:45:22,636 --> 00:45:23,971
Wait, really?

660
00:45:24,054 --> 00:45:27,725
I mean, why would her mother
wanna sue us after a successful surgery?

661
00:45:27,808 --> 00:45:29,435
Hyeon-a finally has
some hope for the future.

662
00:45:29,518 --> 00:45:31,895
Hey, what made you like this, Dr. Jo?

663
00:45:31,979 --> 00:45:33,564
Why don't you have
any faith in your patients?

664
00:45:34,648 --> 00:45:37,818
Well, the lack of faith between doctors
and patients is a common occurrence.

665
00:45:38,527 --> 00:45:39,987
That's why the hospital's empty.

666
00:45:44,324 --> 00:45:47,202
Hello? I'm in the hospital yard right now.

667
00:45:48,579 --> 00:45:50,998
Take them all in.
Yeah, no matter what, take them in.

668
00:45:51,081 --> 00:45:53,375
I'll be right there, I'm on my way.
Okay. Gotta go.

669
00:45:53,459 --> 00:45:55,210
Are you serious? You've been suspended.

670
00:45:55,294 --> 00:45:57,921
Well, there was a big fire at
the building near the park intersection.

671
00:45:58,589 --> 00:46:01,300
Well, you know that firefighter
who ends up in our ER a lot?

672
00:46:01,383 --> 00:46:02,509
He should be here any minute.

673
00:46:02,593 --> 00:46:05,471
Dr. Kim! They're gonna take
more disciplinary action against you.

674
00:46:05,554 --> 00:46:07,306
Whatever, whatever.
They can suspend me, I gotta go!

675
00:46:10,809 --> 00:46:12,519
The cafeteria's serving <i>donkkaseu.</i>

676
00:46:13,353 --> 00:46:15,189
Does this mean I can't have any?

677
00:46:19,526 --> 00:46:20,944
- Um…
- What?

678
00:46:21,528 --> 00:46:24,823
- Are you getting some donkkaseu?
- I won't be able to check up on Hyeon-a.

679
00:46:24,907 --> 00:46:26,116
I can't let that happen.

680
00:46:26,950 --> 00:46:31,121
Come with me.
I got fired, but you only got suspended.

681
00:46:31,205 --> 00:46:33,248
Okay, I'll be right there.

682
00:46:33,332 --> 00:46:34,458
Hmm.

683
00:46:34,541 --> 00:46:36,710
Even on suspension, duty calls.

684
00:47:33,141 --> 00:47:36,061
BONGBONG AUTO REPAIR SHOP

685
00:47:40,065 --> 00:47:41,358
11:30 A. M.
MONDAY, MAY 4

686
00:47:49,241 --> 00:47:51,159
SEMINAR ROOM

687
00:47:52,411 --> 00:47:55,706
Yesterday I was so happy
when we were eating <i>tteokbokki.</i>

688
00:47:55,789 --> 00:47:58,792
I think the meeting's going on right now.
Do we wait for them to invite us in?

689
00:47:58,876 --> 00:47:59,835
I don't know.

690
00:48:01,169 --> 00:48:02,254
Is the meeting over?

691
00:48:02,337 --> 00:48:04,798
Yes, it's over.
It was a very quick meeting.

692
00:48:04,882 --> 00:48:06,884
Well, then why did they tell us to come…

693
00:48:08,677 --> 00:48:09,887
Oh, my goodness.

694
00:48:11,513 --> 00:48:12,347
Here they come.

695
00:48:12,431 --> 00:48:15,976
The heroes from yesterday's
extraordinary surgery are all here.

696
00:48:16,059 --> 00:48:17,269
Have a seat, everyone.

697
00:48:29,698 --> 00:48:31,158
Now, what on earth made you all do that?

698
00:48:31,241 --> 00:48:33,535
If you've already
decided that we are to blame,

699
00:48:34,578 --> 00:48:36,204
then what was the point of summoning us?

700
00:48:36,288 --> 00:48:40,292
Well, I heard you were right outside,
so I thought we should tell you in person

701
00:48:40,375 --> 00:48:42,294
about the board's decision.

702
00:48:42,377 --> 00:48:44,463
So, our determination

703
00:48:44,546 --> 00:48:47,132
was that this surgery
was forced through despite the risks,

704
00:48:47,215 --> 00:48:48,800
and there was a significant chance

705
00:48:48,884 --> 00:48:52,512
that multiple things could have gone
terribly wrong for the patient.

706
00:48:52,596 --> 00:48:54,932
The IRB was already aware of those risks,

707
00:48:55,015 --> 00:48:57,768
which is why they kept
pushing back the meeting.

708
00:48:57,851 --> 00:48:59,811
And we could have had
a discussion about all that

709
00:48:59,895 --> 00:49:01,313
if you had called the meeting sooner.

710
00:49:01,396 --> 00:49:04,232
However,
you chose to do the surgery anyway,

711
00:49:04,316 --> 00:49:06,276
thereby putting the patient in danger.

712
00:49:06,360 --> 00:49:09,738
And you had an outside medical
professional participate in the surgery.

713
00:49:09,821 --> 00:49:11,281
That's another issue we had to consider.

714
00:49:11,365 --> 00:49:13,408
As the director,
I approved her being there.

715
00:49:13,492 --> 00:49:15,160
We took that into account, believe me.

716
00:49:15,953 --> 00:49:19,414
And the fact is
that you barely know that person, huh?

717
00:49:19,498 --> 00:49:22,834
Who do you think you are compromising
the sanctity of the operating room?

718
00:49:22,918 --> 00:49:25,128
Unbelievable.

719
00:49:25,212 --> 00:49:27,422
You were all temporarily suspended
from your duties

720
00:49:27,506 --> 00:49:30,842
based on the reasonable suspicion
that you might repeat the same actions

721
00:49:30,926 --> 00:49:33,053
while awaiting the outcome
of this meeting.

722
00:49:33,136 --> 00:49:36,181
Except that you continued to work,
Dr. Kim Seong-jin.

723
00:49:36,264 --> 00:49:39,393
There was a patient in critical condition.
Was I just supposed to do nothing?

724
00:49:39,476 --> 00:49:42,437
With the staff being limited,
who'll pick up the slack

725
00:49:42,521 --> 00:49:45,315
if doctors trying to do their jobs
all end up getting suspended?

726
00:49:45,399 --> 00:49:46,942
As for you, Dr. Jo Won-jin,

727
00:49:47,985 --> 00:49:50,696
as soon as you heard about the surgery,
you started to organize it

728
00:49:50,779 --> 00:49:53,281
and prepare for it with Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

729
00:49:53,365 --> 00:49:56,576
It seems that you always intended
to perform this surgery.

730
00:49:57,661 --> 00:49:59,579
Same goes for you, Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

731
00:50:00,414 --> 00:50:04,751
Yeah, I assisted in the operation
and I have no regrets about it.

732
00:50:06,586 --> 00:50:07,671
No regrets about it?

733
00:50:08,755 --> 00:50:12,259
Dr. Do, Dr. Bae. Do you feel the same way?

734
00:50:13,552 --> 00:50:16,513
We did the surgery
because it was the patient's last resort.

735
00:50:16,596 --> 00:50:20,559
It was an extremely urgent matter and
a desperate attempt to save a girl's life.

736
00:50:20,642 --> 00:50:23,729
All of us here realize that we must take
responsibility for the outcome,

737
00:50:23,812 --> 00:50:27,482
whatever it may be, but please consider
that a child's life was at stake--

738
00:50:27,566 --> 00:50:29,776
Director Bu Seung-gwon, relieved of duty.

739
00:50:30,402 --> 00:50:33,071
Dr. Do Yun-sik, two-month suspension.

740
00:50:33,155 --> 00:50:35,532
Dr. Bae Heung-gon, one-month suspension.

741
00:50:35,615 --> 00:50:37,784
Dr. Jo Won-jin, three-month suspension.

742
00:50:37,868 --> 00:50:40,203
Dr. Kim Seong-jin, one-month suspension.

743
00:50:40,287 --> 00:50:43,498
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong,
two-month suspension. And--

744
00:50:43,582 --> 00:50:44,916
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong is an intern.

745
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:47,044
A two-month suspension is a heavy penalty.

746
00:50:47,127 --> 00:50:49,755
It's unfair to punish an intern like that
when time constraints

747
00:50:49,838 --> 00:50:52,174
already make it difficult
for him to complete his studies.

748
00:50:52,257 --> 00:50:54,301
Gye Su-jeong.

749
00:50:57,054 --> 00:50:58,388
Your contract is terminated.

750
00:51:02,100 --> 00:51:05,687
You all better hope
that nothing goes wrong with that child,

751
00:51:05,771 --> 00:51:08,148
- because that girl--
- Hyeon-a.

752
00:51:10,400 --> 00:51:11,818
Lee Hyeon-a.

753
00:51:12,944 --> 00:51:15,947
Whether the child dies or lives,
had no bearing on our decision.

754
00:51:16,031 --> 00:51:18,033
This is only about medical ethics.

755
00:51:18,116 --> 00:51:21,578
We focused on whether or not
we can say that the reckless surgery

756
00:51:21,661 --> 00:51:24,623
you forcibly performed
at the risk of the patient's life

757
00:51:24,706 --> 00:51:27,793
was truly, purely, and solely
for the patient.

758
00:51:29,336 --> 00:51:30,837
But most important,

759
00:51:30,921 --> 00:51:33,840
we're doing this before an investigation
by the health authorities,

760
00:51:33,924 --> 00:51:35,342
so just accept that.

761
00:51:36,093 --> 00:51:38,261
There's enough turmoil going on
with the strike,

762
00:51:38,345 --> 00:51:40,931
so let's wrap this up here
before they find fault with us

763
00:51:41,014 --> 00:51:42,599
and start digging things up.

764
00:51:46,937 --> 00:51:49,022
Uh, Dr. Bu Seung-gwon.

765
00:51:49,106 --> 00:51:50,023
What do you think?

766
00:51:50,107 --> 00:51:51,983
Wanna use that back door when you leave?

767
00:51:52,067 --> 00:51:53,610
It'll be your last chance.

768
00:51:53,693 --> 00:51:55,821
You should see what it feels like.

769
00:51:58,198 --> 00:51:59,491
Unbelievable.

770
00:52:00,242 --> 00:52:02,619
- Oh! Uh, oh…
- Oh, what's this?

771
00:52:03,453 --> 00:52:05,080
Is the meeting over already?

772
00:52:06,331 --> 00:52:08,708
Oh, it sounded like fun.
Too bad I missed it.

773
00:52:08,792 --> 00:52:09,626
You are…

774
00:52:09,709 --> 00:52:13,672
Ah. Hello there.
Jang Hui-suk. Here's my card.

775
00:52:14,673 --> 00:52:16,508
Oh, the melon?

776
00:52:17,634 --> 00:52:18,844
If you ever crave a melon,

777
00:52:18,927 --> 00:52:21,138
or you happen to be looking for a job,

778
00:52:21,221 --> 00:52:23,223
keep my business card handy.

779
00:52:25,767 --> 00:52:28,603
Ah, may I introduce
Miss Lee Hyeon-a's mother.

780
00:52:29,229 --> 00:52:33,650
- Oh, hello. Pleased to meet you.
- Nice to meet you. We should be going.

781
00:52:33,733 --> 00:52:35,944
- Yes.
- Excuse me.

782
00:52:36,027 --> 00:52:37,946
Are you taking disciplinary action?

783
00:52:38,029 --> 00:52:42,242
My goodness, ma'am, what you went through
must've been very difficult.

784
00:52:42,325 --> 00:52:44,161
We've reached
a decision on disciplinary action.

785
00:52:44,244 --> 00:52:45,954
Now you just need to focus on your child.

786
00:52:46,037 --> 00:52:48,665
- If you'll excuse us, we're a bit busy so…
- Goodbye.

787
00:52:48,748 --> 00:52:53,170
Today's disciplinary action signifies
that it was an extremely dangerous surgery

788
00:52:53,920 --> 00:52:56,423
and should not have
been performed, doesn't it?

789
00:52:56,506 --> 00:52:58,550
That's true, yeah, basically.

790
00:52:58,633 --> 00:53:00,260
Then I'm going to sue.

791
00:53:10,228 --> 00:53:14,566
I'm going to sue all the doctors who led
and participated in Hyeon-a's surgery.

792
00:53:18,069 --> 00:53:20,155
Oh, of course.

793
00:53:20,238 --> 00:53:23,450
We won't try to stop you
from fighting them in court.

794
00:53:23,533 --> 00:53:26,036
The IRB's opinion is legally binding.

795
00:53:26,828 --> 00:53:29,289
Please just ask us
if you need something, and we can see--

796
00:53:29,372 --> 00:53:31,416
I'll sue Guseo Medical Center
and I'm also going to sue

797
00:53:31,499 --> 00:53:32,959
the Guseo Foundation while I'm at it.

798
00:53:34,794 --> 00:53:38,256
We were originally at the main hospital,
but they sent us to the branch hospital,

799
00:53:38,340 --> 00:53:40,550
saying there was nothing
they could do for her.

800
00:53:40,634 --> 00:53:43,595
It felt like…
they were just dumping us here.

801
00:53:44,387 --> 00:53:47,766
If they hadn't sent us here to avoid
taking responsibility for my child,

802
00:53:47,849 --> 00:53:49,935
she wouldn't have been
put through that surgery.

803
00:53:51,394 --> 00:53:54,481
Well, ma'am, why don't you discuss
this matter with us later--

804
00:53:54,564 --> 00:53:58,735
And I will also-- I will sue the hospital
foundation for one more offense:

805
00:53:58,818 --> 00:54:00,445
for employing a doctor who…

806
00:54:01,279 --> 00:54:03,240
who performs such dangerous operations.

807
00:54:03,323 --> 00:54:05,992
Today's disciplinary action
is proof of that.

808
00:54:10,163 --> 00:54:12,666
But why would I sue Dr. Gye?

809
00:54:12,749 --> 00:54:15,835
She's the one who helped Hyeon-a,
when everyone else wouldn't.

810
00:54:16,920 --> 00:54:19,130
It won't be just her.
Everybody will get sued.

811
00:54:19,214 --> 00:54:22,050
And let them know you'll sue
the foundation and the hospital.

812
00:54:23,343 --> 00:54:24,302
I will?

813
00:54:24,386 --> 00:54:27,597
That way,
Dr. Gye can keep working at this hospital

814
00:54:27,681 --> 00:54:30,558
and also keep an eye on Hyeon-a.

815
00:54:31,977 --> 00:54:35,563
Ma'am, I understand
that you're upset and frustrated, but…

816
00:54:35,647 --> 00:54:38,900
…disgruntled patients
always lose these lawsuits.

817
00:54:40,110 --> 00:54:42,362
It'd be like trying
to break a rock with an egg.

818
00:54:42,445 --> 00:54:44,531
You don't throw
an egg at a rock to break it.

819
00:54:44,614 --> 00:54:45,615
What?

820
00:54:46,408 --> 00:54:49,869
You throw it to get egg all over the rock,
so the stench will begin.

821
00:54:50,996 --> 00:54:54,708
And that stench will get
worse and worse as time goes on,

822
00:54:54,791 --> 00:54:56,584
and become part of the rock.

823
00:54:57,502 --> 00:55:00,046
- Dr. Gye Su-jeong!
- Cleaning it off is impossible.

824
00:55:00,755 --> 00:55:03,383
More eggs will keep being thrown at you.

825
00:55:03,466 --> 00:55:06,511
Soon, people will start pointing
fingers at you, saying…

826
00:55:07,929 --> 00:55:09,055
"That's the place…

827
00:55:10,682 --> 00:55:12,183
where the stench comes from."

828
00:55:18,648 --> 00:55:21,443
Thanks to you,
they put the disciplinary action on hold.

829
00:55:21,526 --> 00:55:22,569
Thank you so much.

830
00:55:23,570 --> 00:55:25,572
But it's only on hold, not withdrawn.

831
00:55:25,655 --> 00:55:29,868
Oh, they just did that to save face.
You don't need to worry.

832
00:55:32,787 --> 00:55:33,913
Thank you very much.

833
00:55:34,539 --> 00:55:40,086
Oh, no, thank you. You-- You saved
my daughter's life, Dr. Gye.

834
00:55:40,962 --> 00:55:42,672
It was the least I could do.

835
00:55:44,549 --> 00:55:45,800
Well, I should go.

836
00:55:50,263 --> 00:55:53,183
Um… Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

837
00:55:54,184 --> 00:55:55,435
Yes?

838
00:55:55,518 --> 00:55:58,146
Would you mind saying
those words to me again?

839
00:55:59,522 --> 00:56:01,983
Of course, given that it was
such a close call with my daughter,

840
00:56:02,650 --> 00:56:05,779
I'm sure those words
won't necessarily always work.

841
00:56:06,529 --> 00:56:08,656
- Still…
- It's okay.

842
00:56:09,324 --> 00:56:10,325
I don't…

843
00:56:12,535 --> 00:56:13,995
I don't ever fail.

844
00:56:19,751 --> 00:56:21,211
Thank you so much.

845
00:56:28,134 --> 00:56:29,302
LEE HYEON-A, F/8

846
00:56:30,387 --> 00:56:34,349
PRIMARY PHYSICIAN: GYE SU-JEONG

847
00:56:34,432 --> 00:56:35,642
MAIN BUILDING WALL CONSTRUCTION

848
00:56:35,725 --> 00:56:37,894
Even though I was
only suspended for one day,

849
00:56:37,977 --> 00:56:41,272
it really made me appreciate just
how much my work means to me, you know.

850
00:56:41,356 --> 00:56:43,149
Although, you did work a little.

851
00:56:43,233 --> 00:56:45,819
Oh, by the way,
most of the firefighters are okay,

852
00:56:45,902 --> 00:56:47,362
except one who's brain-dead.

853
00:56:48,446 --> 00:56:50,698
He signed up to be an organ donor
a long time ago,

854
00:56:50,782 --> 00:56:54,160
and his family knows about it,
so the organ donation coordinator

855
00:56:54,244 --> 00:56:55,745
must've been in touch.

856
00:56:58,623 --> 00:57:01,918
If they have enough money
to print these and put them up,

857
00:57:02,001 --> 00:57:04,421
they probably should've used it
to help finish construction.

858
00:57:06,923 --> 00:57:08,466
What are you doing? Are you coming?

859
00:57:09,342 --> 00:57:10,844
Well, I'm going on ahead.

860
00:57:23,356 --> 00:57:27,986
"Gu Yeo-rim
was the founding director of Guseo--"

861
00:57:28,445 --> 00:57:30,989
"Guseo…" Huh?

862
00:57:31,531 --> 00:57:33,908
"Guseo Medical Center."

863
00:57:34,534 --> 00:57:37,829
- "Paved the way for…"
- "Women."

864
00:57:37,912 --> 00:57:40,331
"…for women in medicine…"

865
00:57:40,415 --> 00:57:44,794
"Expanded gynecological care."

866
00:57:45,545 --> 00:57:47,422
Go on, keep reading.

867
00:57:48,506 --> 00:57:51,050
I learned how to say this in Korean.

868
00:57:51,134 --> 00:57:52,719
Congratulations.

869
00:57:52,802 --> 00:57:55,847
It's been a real privilege
to work with a surgeon like you.

870
00:57:56,848 --> 00:57:59,225
Now you're going back home
to receive a new heart.

871
00:57:59,976 --> 00:58:02,103
Congratulations. I truly mean it.

872
00:58:12,530 --> 00:58:13,740
- <i>Really?</i>
- <i>Yes.</i>

873
00:58:13,823 --> 00:58:15,325
Whoa, then…

874
00:58:15,408 --> 00:58:17,619
He'll be coming here
soon to get the transplant.

875
00:58:18,244 --> 00:58:21,623
Wow. Oh, man, I can't believe
I'll get to meet him in person.

876
00:58:21,748 --> 00:58:24,167
Yeah, but why is he coming here, though?

877
00:58:24,250 --> 00:58:25,793
He could get it done anywhere.

878
00:58:25,877 --> 00:58:29,005
Well, why not?
Our hospital's just as good as any other.

879
00:58:39,307 --> 00:58:41,309
What's wrong? What is it?

880
00:58:41,976 --> 00:58:44,646
What? Did something happen to Su-jeong?

881
00:59:10,463 --> 00:59:12,090
<i>Who is that old man?</i>

882
00:59:13,049 --> 00:59:14,217
"Kim Seung-hyo."

883
00:59:14,300 --> 00:59:17,595
"A general surgeon
who graduated from Guseo University,

884
00:59:17,679 --> 00:59:21,933
and the founder of White Wings,
a medical volunteer organization."

885
00:59:22,016 --> 00:59:25,520
"He provided humanitarian aid
through medical expertise

886
00:59:25,603 --> 00:59:27,480
to impoverished countries,

887
00:59:27,564 --> 00:59:29,816
and was even nominated
for the Nobel Prize."

888
00:59:29,899 --> 00:59:33,570
"He has saved countless children with
his exceptional medical skill,

889
00:59:33,653 --> 00:59:38,199
and is praised as a great, benevolent
healer of our age, even revered as a god."

890
00:59:38,992 --> 00:59:40,535
All right, let's go.

891
00:59:41,619 --> 00:59:43,538
Goodness, Ga-eul, that was amazing.

892
00:59:46,916 --> 00:59:50,295
KIM SEUNG-HYO
FOUNDER OF WHITE WINGS MEDICAL CORPS

893
00:59:57,010 --> 01:00:01,097
Why does he insist on coming here
to this hospital to have the operation?

894
01:00:01,180 --> 01:00:02,932
It must be hard for him to get around.

895
01:00:03,016 --> 01:00:06,269
Well, he says his guardian and the person
he wants to perform the surgery

896
01:00:06,352 --> 01:00:07,729
are both here at this hospital.

897
01:00:07,812 --> 01:00:09,439
And who would his guardian be?

898
01:00:38,676 --> 01:00:40,678
<i>It's Dr. Jo Won-jin.</i>

899
01:00:42,347 --> 01:00:44,682
Dr. Jo Won-jin, is that right?

900
01:00:44,766 --> 01:00:46,643
And who'll be his primary surgeon?

901
01:00:47,477 --> 01:00:50,772
The same surgeon who did
his initial transplant operation.

902
01:00:57,278 --> 01:00:58,780
<i>Dr. Gye Su-jeong.</i>

903
01:01:02,867 --> 01:01:04,077
Auntie.

904
01:01:04,827 --> 01:01:08,331
Auntie! Auntie, wake up. Please!

905
01:01:08,956 --> 01:01:09,999
Auntie!

906
01:01:58,297 --> 01:02:00,258
TWO DAYS LATER

907
01:02:00,925 --> 01:02:04,595
PATIENT: KIM SEUNG-HYO
PRIMARY SURGEON: GYE SU-JEONG

908
01:02:22,321 --> 01:02:24,741
PATIENT: KIM SEUNG-HYO
PRIMARY SURGEON: GYE SU-JEONG

909
01:02:59,150 --> 01:03:00,067
Park Tae-gyeong.

910
01:03:02,111 --> 01:03:03,112
Park Tae-gyeong!

911
01:03:28,179 --> 01:03:29,847
It's been a while…

912
01:03:33,309 --> 01:03:35,228
Doctor X.

913
01:03:48,616 --> 01:03:51,577
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

914
01:04:30,700 --> 01:04:33,661
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

915
01:04:34,245 --> 01:04:35,621
<i>It's been a while, sir.</i>

916
01:04:35,705 --> 01:04:37,498
<i>All I did was watch,</i>

917
01:04:37,582 --> 01:04:40,126
<i>but you saved his life again, Dr. Gye.</i>

918
01:04:40,209 --> 01:04:43,004
<i>I heard Dr. Kim Seung-hyo</i>
<i>personally chose Gye Su-jeong.</i>

919
01:04:43,087 --> 01:04:45,047
Who in the world is Gye Su-jeong?

920
01:04:45,131 --> 01:04:47,258
<i>Apparently, he told them to come.</i>

921
01:04:47,341 --> 01:04:49,010
<i>To all the kids I met back then…</i>

922
01:04:50,469 --> 01:04:52,680
<i>Dad is a monster.</i>

923
01:04:52,763 --> 01:04:54,432
Please come here right now. Please!

924
01:04:54,515 --> 01:04:55,892
<i>Um, Dr. Gye?</i>

925
01:04:56,767 --> 01:04:58,060
<i>Could you…</i>

926
01:04:58,811 --> 01:05:00,313
<i>just this one time, fail?</i>
